user:
Generate an adjuster memo narrative comparing these two estimates.

Primary Estimate: {primary_name}
Comparison Estimate: {comparison_name}

Analysis Results:
Overall Direction: {overall_delta_direction}
Confidence: {confidence}

Category Analyses:
{category_analyses_json}

Scope Gaps Identified:
{scope_gaps_json}

Respond with JSON matching this exact structure:
{{
  "overview": "2-3 sentences: (1) Total delta direction and magnitude between {primary_name} and {comparison_name}. (2) Primary causes of the difference. (3) Key assumptions or reasoning behind the delta.",
  "key_drivers": [
    {{
      "category": "category name",
      "amounts": "$X vs $Y (delta $Z)",
      "narrative": "Two sentences: (1) State delta amount/direction. (2) Identify primary cause."
    }}
  ],
  "scope_observations": ["Specific scope item missing or different", "Another scope observation"],
  "suggested_followups": ["Request itemized breakdown of X", "Clarify Y methodology"]
}}

Rules:
- overview: 2-3 sentences covering delta magnitude, primary causes, and key assumptions
- key_drivers: One entry per significant category delta, use comparative framing
- amounts: Always format as "$X vs $Y (delta $Z)" or "{primary_name}: $X. {comparison_name}: $Y."
- narrative: EXACTLY two sentences per driver: (1) delta assessment, (2) cause analysis
- scope_observations: Specific items, not vague statements
- suggested_followups: Actionable items for resolution
- Always use estimate names ({primary_name} and {comparison_name}) in comparative framing
